a()`, verify that `initializeValidators()` is invoked twice (once per list entry), confirming that the method does not deduplicate entries."}]}, {'group': 'Null schema element', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NullPointerException thrown when iterating over a null element in `schemas`.', 'description': "Insert a `null` reference into the validator's `schemas` list (e.g., `[mockSchema, null, mockSchema]`). Calling `preloadJsonSchema()` should result in a NullPointerException when the for‑each loop attempts to call `initializeValidators()` on the null element, demonstrating that the method does not guard against null entries."}]}, {'group': 'Concurrent modification during iteration', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'ConcurrentModificationException propagates out of preloadJsonSchema.', 'description': "Configure a mock JsonSchema whose `initializeValidators()` method adds another JsonSchema to the validator's `schemas` list. When `preloadJsonSchema()` runs, the underlying `ArrayList` will detect the structural modification during iteration and throw a ConcurrentModificationException, confirming that the method does not protect against concurrent modifications."}]}, {'group': 'Idempotent call', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'initializeValidators called exactly once per schema on each invocation; no side‑effects beyond the calls.', 'description': "Add three distinct mock JsonSchema objects to the validator's `schemas` list. Invoke `preloadJsonSchema()` twice in succession. Verify that `initializeValidators()` is called three times after the first call and three additional times after the second call (total six), demonstrating that the method can be safely called multiple times."}]}]
